[0.003, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[18D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[15A\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;175;175;175m❯ \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mI think we should do all this stuff single-user for now and worry about users later.\u001b[39m                                  \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mI don't want to have the user curating their categories from a dedicated UI as the main mode of adding them.\u001b[39m          \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mI think there's a big UX consideration here – we should probably make the category box in the receipt item list be \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mone of those pop-down boxes where it's a filterable select (like you type and it narrows to the matching set), with a\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m clear \"Create new category\" option that works with the current text.\u001b[39m                                                "]
[0.000, "o", " \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mThen I guess we can do the standard create/read/update/delete endpoints, but the main way the user accesses them is \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mthrough there. So #2 with an eye towards that UI.\u001b[39m                                                                     \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mAny db/representational concerns with that UI?\u001b[39m                                                                        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m   \u001b[1C                   \u001b[1C        \u001b[1C    \u001b[1C    \u001b[1C   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✢\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mCrunching… \u001b[39m                                                                                                           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  ⎿  Tip: Create skills by adding .md files to .claude/skills/ in y"]
