[0.814, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[2D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[4A  \u001b[1m1. Implicit creation needs normalization.\u001b[22m The \"create new from typed text\" path means every keystroke quirk becomes a \r\u001b[1B  candidate\u001b[1Centry:\u001b[1C\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m\"Groceries \"\u001b[39m,\u001b[1C\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m\"groceries\"\u001b[39m,\u001b[1C\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m\"Groceries\"\u001b[39m.\u001b[1CTrim\u001b[1C+\u001b[1Ccase-insensitive\u001b[1Cuniqueness\u001b[1Con\u001b[1Cthe\u001b[1CPK\u001b[1C(\u001b[38;2;87;105;247mCOLLATE NOCASE\u001b[39m)\r\u001b[1B   handles it. Open question: do you preserve the user's casing for display (store what they first typed) or force Title\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B Case? I'd preserve\u001b[1C—\u001b[1Cfeels\u001b[1Cless\u001b[1Cpaternalistic\u001b[1Cin\u001b[1Ca\u001b[1Csingle-user\u001b[1Ctool.\u001b[26C                     \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
