[0.838, "o", "\u001b]0;⠂ Integrate user category feedback into prompts\u0007"]
[0.005, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[60D\u001b[3B\r\u001b[17A\u001b[48;2;240;240;240m\u001b[38;2;175;175;175m❯ \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mReactions:\u001b[39m                                                                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m1. Trim + case seems good. Agree on store what the user typed\u001b[39m                                                         \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m2. \"Create new\" in the category box should be 'category/add' + 'receipt/update', yes?\u001b[39m                                 \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m3. That's interesting. There's a gotcha there where if you mis-categorize as \"Misc\" and then switch it you have to \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mretype \"Misc\" on the item you mean to use. I think that's probably fine.\u001b[39m                                              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m4. That's interesting. Easiest is to have a \"Unassigned\" category that can't go away IMO\u001b[39m             "]
[0.000, "o", "                 \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m5. I wonder about having a link button on each category that jumps to the category page. Has stats + renamability.\u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m6. Yeah I almost wonder about allowing the prompt to come up with categories outside the given set, and having no \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mseed?\u001b[39m                                                                                                                 \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0m7. Yeah there are no external users of these libraries yet, but thanks for flagging\u001b[39m                                   \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mOne other consideration – there will be a lot of duplicated strings with this approach. Should Category be a table \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;0;0;0mwith an id and a foreign key from receiptitem to category?\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m    \u001b[1C"]
[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[1C  \u001b[1C   \u001b[1C \u001b[1C       \u001b[1C   \u001b[1C    \u001b[1C           \u001b[1C  \u001b[1C          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✽\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;215;119;87mEnchanting… \u001b[39m                                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m  ⎿  Tip: Use /agents to optimize specific tasks. Eg. Software Architect, Code Writer, Code Reviewer\u001b[39m                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
